course: dictionary
lesson: 6391
title: One word, many meanings: mum
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find out which one is meant. «Megan could say calmly, "My mum cares for my brother."» A mum cares for a child, so here mum means mother.
explain: Some words sit in set phrases. «Keep mum» means keep quiet and say nothing. Ask yourself: does mother fit here? If it does not make sense, look for a phrase, and check the words next to it.
explain: «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» Here Mum is a person in the story, and it starts with a capital letter. Her door tells you this Mum is someone's mother in the house. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Mum means mother, and it is the everyday word in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. In the USA and Canada people say Mom.
fact: In Ireland, Wales and northern England people often say mam, and very small children say mummy.
fact: «Keep mum» means keep quiet and say nothing, as in «Keep mum about the surprise party!»
fact: In playground jokes, «your mum» is a rude put-down that is not about anybody's real mother, so leave it out.
fact: In formal writing, mother, parent or guardian is used instead of mum: «a parent or guardian must sign».
exercise: «Megan could say calmly, "My mum cares for my brother."» What does mum mean here? | Keep quiet | *Mother | A flower | A rude joke
exercise: «Keep mum» is a phrase. What does it mean? | *Keep quiet and say nothing | Shout loudly | Keep your mum happy | Go to bed early
exercise: A school form is written in formal language. Which word would it use instead of mum? | Mummy | Mom | Keep mum | *Parent
test: «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» What does Mum mean in this sentence? | A flower | Quiet | *A mother | A joke
test: Which everyday word for mother is used in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand? | Mom | Momma | Madam | *Mum
exam: In «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law», what does mother-in-law mean? | A cousin | *The mother of your husband or wife | Your own mother | A flower
